      "id": 1,
      "text": "Exeter was laid out in June 1825, making it the oldest town in Scott County, and was named after Exeter, New Hampshire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/exeter_illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pioneer arrivals began around 1820 after the 1819 Kickapoo treaty, and James Mills founded the first mill in 1821.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/exeter_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1838 the Potawatomi Trail of Death passed through Exeter, marking a tragic chapter in the region’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exeter%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Exeter is part of the Jacksonville Micropolitan Statistical Area, linking it to a broader regional economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
